## Micro-Frontend Consistency Strategy

### Shared Component Library
- **Scope**: Atomic components (Button, Input, Select, Modal, etc.)
- **Distribution**: NPM package `@company/design-system`
- **Versioning**: Semantic versioning, support N-1 major version
- **Documentation**: Storybook hosted at design.company.com

### Integration Patterns
| Pattern | Use Case | Consistency Mechanism |
|---------|----------|----------------------|
| Build-Time Integration | Static content, low change frequency | Shared component library, compile together |
| Run-Time Integration | Dynamic content, independent deployments | Web Components, shared CSS variables |
| Server-Side Composition | SEO-critical pages | Template inheritance, shared CSS |

### Cross-Team Governance
- **Design System Council**: 1 rep from each team, meet monthly
- **Contribution Model**: Any team can propose components, council reviews/approves
- **Breaking Changes**: 3-month deprecation notice, migration guide required
- **Component Lifecycle**: Experimental → Beta → Stable → Deprecated

## Complex Web Accessibility Patterns

### Accessible Rich Internet Applications (ARIA)
| Component | Role | State | Properties | Keyboard |
|-----------|------|-------|-----------|----------|
| Tab Panel | `tab`, `tabpanel` | `aria-selected` | `aria-controls` | Arrow keys, Home, End |
| Dropdown Menu | `menu`, `menuitem` | `aria-expanded` | `aria-haspopup` | Arrow keys, Esc |
| Modal Dialog | `dialog` | `aria-hidden` | `aria-labelledby`, `aria-describedby` | Tab trap, Esc to close |
| Tree View | `tree`, `treeitem` | `aria-expanded` | `aria-level`, `aria-posinset` | Arrow keys, Enter |
| Combobox (Autocomplete) | `combobox`, `listbox` | `aria-expanded` | `aria-autocomplete` | Arrow keys, Esc, Enter |

### Focus Management for SPAs
- **Route Changes**: Move focus to `<h1>` or skip-link
- **Modal Open**: Trap focus within modal, restore on close
- **Dynamic Content**: Announce via `aria-live` regions
- **Infinite Scroll**: Manage focus after load, don't lose position

### Performance Budget for Complex UIs
| Metric | Budget | Rationale |
|--------|--------|-----------|
| Time to Interactive (TTI) | <3.5s on 3G | User engagement threshold |
| First Contentful Paint (FCP) | <1.5s | Perceived performance |
| Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) | <2.5s | Core Web Vitals |
| Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) | <0.1 | Visual stability |
| Total Bundle Size (JS) | <300KB gzipped | Mobile data constraints |
| Animation Frame Rate | 60 FPS | Smooth interactions |

## Complex Web UI Patterns

### Infinite Scroll vs Pagination
| Consideration | Infinite Scroll | Pagination |
|---------------|----------------|------------|
| Use Case | Social feeds, image galleries | Search results, tables |
| Accessibility | ❌ Challenging (focus, back button) | ✅ Straightforward |
| Performance | ⚠️ Memory accumulation | ✅ Fixed cost per page |
| SEO | ❌ Content not indexed | ✅ All pages indexable |

**UX Recommendation**: Pagination for data-heavy apps, infinite scroll for engagement-focused apps (with accessibility fallback).

### Data Table Design (Enterprise Scale)

#### Requirements for 10K+ Row Tables
- **Virtualization**: Render only visible rows (react-window, ag-Grid)
- **Column Management**: User can show/hide, reorder, resize columns
- **Sorting**: Multi-column sort with visual indicators
- **Filtering**: Per-column filters (text, date range, dropdown)
- **Selection**: Bulk selection with "Select All" (current page vs all pages)
- **Export**: CSV/Excel export with current filters applied
- **Responsive**: Collapse to cards on mobile

#### Accessibility for Data Tables
- `<table>`, `<thead>`, `<tbody>`, `<th scope="col">` (semantic HTML)
- Sort buttons in column headers with `aria-sort="ascending"`
- Filter inputs labeled with `aria-label`
- Selected rows indicated visually + `aria-selected="true"`
- Keyboard navigation: Arrow keys between cells, Tab for interactive elements

## Complex Web User Stories

**US-CW-UX-001: Component Library Documentation**
As a frontend developer in a micro-frontend team
I want interactive component documentation with code examples
So that I can integrate components without guessing

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Storybook deployed at design.company.com
- [ ] Every component has: Overview, Props API, Examples, Accessibility notes
- [ ] Code snippets copyable (React, Vue, vanilla JS)
- [ ] Visual regression tests run on every component change
- [ ] Search functionality to find components by name/tag

**US-CW-UX-002: Consistent Navigation Across Micro-Frontends**
As a user navigating between different parts of the app
I want the navigation bar to remain consistent
So that I'm not confused by layout shifts

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Shell app owns global navigation component
- [ ] Micro-frontends communicate active route to shell
- [ ] Navigation highlights current section
- [ ] No flash/jump during route transitions
- [ ] Mobile: Hamburger menu, tablet/desktop: horizontal nav

