# Mobile Application UX Principles

## Platform-Native Design Guidelines

### iOS Human Interface Guidelines (HIG)
| Component | iOS Pattern | Don't Do | Why |
|-----------|-------------|----------|-----|
| Navigation | Bottom tab bar (5 max) | Hamburger menu | Thumb zone optimization |
| Actions | Swipe gestures (delete, archive) | Hidden menus | Discoverability |
| Confirmation | Action sheet (bottom) | Alert dialog for every action | Reduces friction |
| Back Navigation | Swipe from left edge | Back button only | Native gesture |
| System Fonts | SF Pro, SF Compact | Custom fonts everywhere | Readability |

### Android Material Design Guidelines
| Component | Android Pattern | Don't Do | Why |
|-----------|----------------|----------|-----|
| Navigation | Bottom nav OR nav drawer | Both simultaneously | Consistency |
| Primary Action | Floating Action Button (FAB) | FAB for every screen | Overuse dilutes importance |
| Snackbar | Temporary feedback (bottom) | Toast for critical info | Accessibility |
| Back Navigation | System back button | Custom back behavior | User expectation |
| Typography | Roboto font family | iOS-style fonts | Platform consistency |

## Touch Target Specifications

### Minimum Touch Target Sizes
- **iOS**: 44×44 pt minimum (Apple HIG)
- **Android**: 48×48 dp minimum (Material Design)
- **Recommendation**: 48×48 dp / 44×44 pt for cross-platform consistency

### Thumb Zone Optimization (One-Handed Use)
```
┌─────────────────────┐
│   ❌ Hard to Reach   │ ← Top of screen
│                     │
│   ⚠️ Stretch Zone    │ ← Middle
│                     │
│   ✅ Easy Reach      │ ← Bottom (navigation, primary actions)
└─────────────────────┘
```

**Design Implication**: 
- Primary actions at bottom (thumb-friendly)
- Secondary actions at top (intentional friction)
- Swipe gestures for efficiency (less precise targeting)

## Gesture Design Patterns

### Standard Gestures (Don't Reinvent)
| Gesture | Action | Use Case |
|---------|--------|----------|
| Tap | Primary action | Select item, press button |
| Long Press | Secondary action / context menu | Delete, share, more options |
| Swipe Horizontal | Navigate or reveal actions | Swipe to delete, swipe between tabs |
| Swipe Vertical | Scroll | Feed browsing |
| Pinch | Zoom | Image viewer, maps |
| Pull-to-Refresh | Reload content | Feeds, lists |
| Swipe from Edge | System navigation | Back (left edge), forward (right edge) |

### Custom Gesture Guidelines
- **Teach First**: Show gesture hint on first use (e.g., "Swipe left to archive")
- **Visible Affordance**: Show partial reveal to hint at action
- **Immediate Feedback**: Visual response within 100ms
- **Undo Support**: Easy undo for destructive gestures

## Mobile Accessibility (VoiceOver / TalkBack)

### Screen Reader Optimization
| Element | Accessibility Requirement | Implementation |
|---------|--------------------------|----------------|
| Button | Descriptive label, role | `accessibilityLabel="Add to cart"`, `accessibilityRole="button"` |
| Image | Alt text (decorative: empty) | `accessibilityLabel="Product photo"` or `accessibilityLabel=""` |
| Input | Label + hint | `accessibilityLabel="Email"`, `accessibilityHint="Enter your email address"` |
| Status Update | Announce dynamically | `accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"` (Android), `accessibilityTraits="updatesFrequently"` (iOS) |
| Navigation | Announce route changes | Use React Navigation's `screenOptions.title` |

### Voice Control (iOS) / Voice Access (Android)
- All interactive elements must have unique, speakable labels
- Example: "Tap Add to Cart" should work (avoid "Tap Button 3")

### Dynamic Type Support (iOS) / Font Scaling (Android)
- Support system font size preferences (up to 300% scaling)
- Test at largest accessibility size: Text should remain readable, not truncated
- Use scalable units: SP (Android), points with Dynamic Type (iOS)

## Mobile Performance UX

### Perceived Performance Techniques
| Technique | Description | Use Case |
|-----------|-------------|----------|
| Skeleton Screens | Show layout with placeholders | Feed loading |
| Optimistic UI | Show result before server confirms | Like button, quick actions |
| Progressive Image Loading | Low-res → High-res | Image galleries |
| Lazy Loading | Load content as user scrolls | Long lists |
| Prefetching | Load next screen in background | Predicted navigation |

### Battery & Memory Optimization (UX Impact)
- **Animations**: Reduce or disable on low battery mode
- **Background Sync**: Defer non-critical updates
- **Image Resolution**: Serve smaller images on low-end devices
- **Video Autoplay**: Disable on cellular (data cost UX)

## Mobile Form Design

### Mobile-Optimized Input Fields
| Input Type | Keyboard Type | Input Mode | Autocomplete |
|------------|---------------|------------|--------------|
| Email | Email keyboard | `email` | `email` |
| Phone | Numeric keyboard | `tel` | `tel` |
| Credit Card | Numeric keyboard | `numeric` | `cc-number` |
| Postal Code | Alphanumeric | `postal-code` | `postal-code` |
| Password | Default | `text` (with hide/show toggle) | `current-password` |

### Mobile Form Best Practices
- **One Input per Screen**: Reduces cognitive load (especially onboarding)
- **Input Masks**: Format as user types (e.g., phone: `(555) 123-4567`)
- **Floating Labels**: Label moves up when focused (saves vertical space)
- **Inline Validation**: Real-time feedback on blur (not on every keystroke)
- **Clear Error Messages**: "Email format invalid" (not "Invalid input")
- **Autocomplete**: Use browser autofill for name, address, payment

## Mobile User Stories

**US-MOB-UX-001: Gesture-Based Navigation**
As a mobile user browsing a feed
I want swipe gestures for common actions
So that I can act quickly without precise taps

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Swipe right on item: "Archive" (with undo)
- [ ] Swipe left on item: "Delete" (with confirmation)
- [ ] Long press: Show context menu with all actions
- [ ] Visual feedback: Item slides with gesture (immediate response)
- [ ] Accessibility: Actions also available via buttons for screen reader users

**US-MOB-UX-002: Dark Mode Support**
As a mobile user who browses at night
I want dark mode that respects system settings
So that my eyes aren't strained

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Auto-detect system dark mode preference
- [ ] Manual toggle in settings (override system)
- [ ] All screens support dark mode (no blinding white flashes)
- [ ] Colors: Pure black (#000) for OLED battery savings
- [ ] Contrast: WCAG AA in dark mode (4.5:1 text, 3:1 UI)
- [ ] Images: Optionally dim or invert colors

**US-MOB-UX-003: Offline Mode UI**
As a mobile user on a subway with no signal
I want clear indication of what works offline
So that I don't attempt impossible actions

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Offline banner: "You're offline. Some features unavailable."
- [ ] Disabled actions: Greyed out with tooltip "Requires internet"
- [ ] Cached content: Clearly marked "Last updated: 2 hours ago"
- [ ] Queue pending actions: "Will send when online" status
