# Internationalization UX Strategy

## Right-to-Left (RTL) Design

### RTL Languages
- **Primary**: Arabic, Hebrew, Persian (Farsi), Urdu
- **User Base**: 500M+ people

### RTL Layout Mirroring

**What to Mirror**:
- Overall page layout (sidebar left → right)
- Navigation (menu icon, breadcrumbs)
- Reading order (left-to-right → right-to-left)
- Arrows (back → forward, next → previous)
- Checkboxes, radio buttons (right-aligned)

**What NOT to Mirror**:
- Numbers (always LTR: "123" not "321")
- Phone numbers, dates in LTR format
- Media controls (play icon: ▶ universal)
- Charts, graphs (X-axis left-to-right by convention)
- Brand logos

### RTL Implementation (CSS)
```css
/* Automatic RTL with logical properties (IE11+: fallback required) */
.container {
  padding-left: 16px;           /* Fallback for older browsers */
  padding-right: 16px;
  padding-inline-start: 16px;   /* Modern: Start edge (left LTR, right RTL) */
  padding-inline-end: 16px;     /* Modern: End edge */
  margin-inline-start: auto;
}

/* Manual RTL */
[dir="rtl"] .sidebar {
  right: 0;  /* Instead of left: 0 */
}

[dir="rtl"] .icon-arrow {
  transform: scaleX(-1);  /* Flip horizontally */
}
```

### RTL Testing Checklist
- [ ] All text aligns right (not left)
- [ ] Scroll bars appear on left side
- [ ] Forms labels right-aligned
- [ ] Tooltips appear on correct side
- [ ] Animations flow right-to-left
- [ ] No text overflow or truncation

## Text Expansion Handling

### Language Expansion Rates (vs English)
| Language | Expansion | Example: "Submit" |
|----------|-----------|-------------------|
| English | 100% (baseline) | Submit (6 chars) |
| German | +30% | Einreichen (10 chars) |
| French | +20% | Soumettre (9 chars) |
| Spanish | +15% | Enviar (6 chars) |
| Italian | +20% | Invia (5 chars) |
| Portuguese | +25% | Submeter (8 chars) |
| Russian | -10% | Отправить (9 chars, but wider glyphs) |

### Design for Text Expansion
- **Buttons**: Min-width 120px, avoid fixed width
- **Navigation**: Horizontal nav may wrap, consider dropdown
- **Tables**: Column headers may need 2 lines
- **Forms**: Labels above inputs (not beside) for long translations
- **Tooltips**: Max-width with word wrap

### CSS Strategies
```css
/* Flexible buttons */
.button {
  min-width: 120px;
  padding: 0.5em 1em;
  white-space: nowrap;
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;  /* Fallback if too long */
}

/* Multi-line labels */
.form-label {
  display: block;
  line-height: 1.4;
  margin-bottom: 0.5em;
}
```

## Cultural Design Patterns

### Color Symbolism by Culture
| Color | Western | Eastern | Middle East | Action |
|-------|---------|---------|-------------|--------|
| Red | Danger, stop | Luck, celebration | Danger | Use with context (not just red for error in China) |
| White | Purity, peace | Death, mourning | Purity | Avoid pure white backgrounds in East Asian funerals context |
| Yellow | Caution | Royalty (China) | Prosperity | Safe for most uses |
| Green | Go, success | Islam, nature | Islam, fertility | Universally positive |
| Blue | Trust, calm | Immortality | Protection | Safest color globally |

### Icon Localization
| Icon | Western Meaning | Issues | Localized Alternative |
|------|----------------|--------|----------------------|
| 👍 Thumbs Up | Like, approve | Offensive in Middle East, Greece | ❤️ Heart (universal) |
| 🙏 Praying Hands | Thank you, please | Religious in some contexts | ✨ Sparkles |
| 📧 Envelope | Email | May not represent local mail system | @ symbol |
| 💵 Dollar Sign | Money | US-centric | Generic coin/currency icon |

### Date & Time Display
| Locale | Date Format | Time Format | First Day of Week |
|--------|-------------|-------------|-------------------|
| en-US | MM/DD/YYYY | 12-hour (AM/PM) | Sunday |
| en-GB | DD/MM/YYYY | 24-hour | Monday |
| de-DE | DD.MM.YYYY | 24-hour | Monday |
| ja-JP | YYYY/MM/DD | 24-hour | Sunday |
| ar-SA | DD/MM/YYYY | 12-hour (AM/PM, use Eastern Arabic numerals: ١٢:٣٠ or Western 0-9) | Saturday |

