## Data Visualization Best Practices

### Chart Selection Guide
| Data Type | Recommended Chart | Avoid | Why |
|-----------|------------------|-------|-----|
| Trend over Time | Line chart | Pie chart | Shows changes clearly |
| Part-to-Whole | Stacked bar, pie (≤5 segments) | 3D pie | Easy comparison |
| Comparison | Bar chart (horizontal if long labels) | Area chart | Clear differences |
| Distribution | Histogram, box plot | Line chart | Shows spread |
| Correlation | Scatter plot | Bar chart | Shows relationships |
| Geographic | Choropleth map | Table | Spatial patterns |

### Color Use in Data Visualization
- **Categorical Data**: Distinct hues (blue, orange, green, red)
- **Sequential Data**: Single hue, varying lightness (light blue → dark blue)
- **Diverging Data**: Two hues from neutral midpoint (red ← gray → green)
- **Accessibility**: Colorblind-safe palettes (use Coblis simulator)
- **Semantic Colors**: Red (bad/down), green (good/up), yellow (warning)

### Enterprise Chart Requirements
- [ ] **Interactivity**: Hover for exact values, click to drill down
- [ ] **Export**: PNG, PDF, CSV (for reports)
- [ ] **Responsive**: Readable on mobile (simplified view if needed)
- [ ] **Real-Time**: WebSocket updates for live dashboards
- [ ] **Performance**: Render 100K+ data points with virtualization

